; Tasks declared by row rather than by a (task ..) head: duties an org assigns
; (org_duties, tables/duty-tables.mc) that no rule performs yet. A duty is a TASK label -
; {@self duty-to ?org [k <duty>]} - so the name is a task term under act > task.
(task dismiss_staff (sub [k human] @object))
(task review_staff (sub [k human] @object))
(task keep_records (sub [k human] @object))
(task provide_for (sub [k human] @object))
(task protect (sub [k human] @object))
(task officiate (sub [k human] @object))
(task admit_member (sub [k human] @object))
; set-mealtimes ?household - fix the household's meal hours; the duty of the woman of the
; house to her household (thinks/cooldown/household-think.mc).
(task set-mealtimes (tar [k household] @object))
; kill and acquire are pursued as intents ({@self intent kill ?victim}): their drivers pick the
; means (thinks/hot/kill-think.mc, thinks/hot/acquire-think.mc) and no task performs them whole.
(task kill (tar [k human] @object))
(task acquire (tar ?))
; get-job is pursued as an intent ({@self intent {@self get-job}}): its driver reads the parish
; board and applies (thinks/hot/job-search-think.mc); taking up an offer performs it.
(task get-job)
